## 2. Container-level notes

* Standard DBPF 1.0 exactly as already handled by `addons/dbpf/DBPF.gd`; the engine's QFS
  decompressor and DIR handling load every subfile in this save without error.
* Almost every savegame subfile lives in group `0x299B2D1B` (121 of 179 entries). The
  exceptions: LTEXTs (`0x6AAEE931/32` name/mayor, `0x4A2482BB` thumbnail labels), PNG
  thumbnails (`0x4A2482BB`), terrain (`0xE98F9525`), the region-view record (`0xCA027EE1`)
  and a handful of singletons.
* Savegame records follow SC4's standard serialization: `u32 size, u32 CRC, u32 memory
  address`, then a version and class-specific payload. 120 of the 133 types chain
  cleanly as size-prefixed record arrays (verified while counting the records above).
* Several network subfiles are **absent from this save** — network subfile 2 (`0xCA16374F`,
  bridges/elevated), the tunnel subfile (`0x8A4BD52B`), the prebuilt network (`0x49C1A034`) and
  the power-line pair (`0xC9C05C5D` / `0x09C05C6A`) — consistent with a flat tutorial city with
  no bridges, tunnels or long-distance power. Other shipped saves do have them: see §4.4.

## 3. Implementation status in OpenSC4 (summary)

**Implemented today (15 of the 133 types present):** building/prop/flora occupants, lots, lot
base textures, terrain altitudes (main map only), region-view stats, PNG thumbnails, LTEXT, the
DIR directory, and — as of 2026-08-06 — the whole of §4.4: ground networks, pipes, the network
index, lot foundations and retaining walls, plus the power-line and bridge subfiles that occur
in other saves. In short: **everything the city renderer needs to draw a complete city, and
nothing of the simulation.**

Prop rendering was completed later the same day. 413 of this save's 69,431 prop occupants
reference no 3D model at all — they are 2D sprites, and were being silently dropped; §8 has the
format and the fix. The 2,339 props still unplaced are a *different* problem: they do name an
S3D model, but no zoom/rotation variant of it exists in the DATs we load.

**Not implemented (present in this save):** the item index, zone developer/manager, tract
developer, every simulator/manager state blob, budget (departments, line
items, taxes), the ~20 ordinances, historical graph data, advice state, and the COM-serializer
registry. (The 136 SimGrid layers, previously on this list, are parsed and modeled now — §11,
§12.)

**Engine scaffolding still unfed:** `CityView/ClassDefinitions/` (NetGraphNode, NetGraphEdge,
NetTile, TransitTile) models a transit-network *graph*. The §4.4 parsers give it geometry but
not connectivity — that needs `SC4Path` (`0x296678F7`), which has no parser. Note
`NeworkGraph.gd` (filename typo intentional) is dead and internally inconsistent
(`tile.networedges` vs `tile.networkedges`); treat it as a sketch, not an API.

Also worth noting: the region UI derives the displayed city name from the *filename*
(`RegionCityView.gd:22`), while the save carries properly localized name/mayor LTEXTs.

