### 0x49D5B964 / 0x49D5B953 are the flammability pair, not pollution

§12 nominated these as the prime air-pollution candidates. Crosstabbing per BUILDING
(not per tile) kills that: `0x49D5B964`'s dominant values are the building exemplars'
`Flammability` property (0x29244DB5) **verbatim** — R$ families 40, dirty industry 80 —
resolved through the family cohort chain, stamped over the lot rect. Exact per-tile
agreement runs 0.66 (Tegel) to 0.95 (Rush Hour) across the populated saves; the shortfall
is small decays (38 where 40 is expected) and lot garden tiles carrying their trees' value.
The twins share one footprint and `0x49D5B964 = 0.8 × 0x49D5B953` within u8 rounding on
≥99% of nonzero cells (85 of 7,816 differ on Big City, where the two are equal instead) —
and 1/0.8 = 1.25 matches the "Flammability multiplier, summer" property family. So:
**base** and **seasonally-multiplied** flammability. Consts + evidence on `SimGridSubfile`,
gates in `_check_flammability_grids` (floors 0.60 exact / 0.98 pair relation).

The pollution properties themselves live on the family cohorts too: "Pollution at centre"
0x27812851 is `[air, water, garbage, radiation]`, SIGNED (trees absorb, −1/−2); "Pollution
Radius" 0x68EE9764 the matching radii in tiles (dirty industry 13–20). Parsing cohorts
needed one `ExemplarSubfile` change: accept signature CQZB alongside EQZB (byte-identical
layouts); `Core.exemplar_prop(group, instance, prop)` walks exemplar → cohort chain with a
flat cache.

### 0x41800000 is the zone-type grid

Crosstab against lot `zone_type` is single-valued on every zone (1→1, 4→4, 8→8, 9→9,
15→15, plus 14 on special-zone tiles no lot claims): the save stores zoning per tile,
verbatim. ≥99.6% agreement on every populated save; const on `SimGridSubfile`, gate in
`_check_zone_grid`. (The dataId is the bit pattern of 16.0f — presumably an accident of
whatever GUID the grid was registered under.)

### 0x49D5BB8C / 0x49D5BBA1: ruled out as crime, not identified

§12's crime candidates. The two are cell-identical on most saves (not all), tiny bitfield
values ({0,2,8,10} on Big City: 2 on developed tiles, 8 along power-line corridors, 10
both), which read as power — but only 19% of Tegel's lot tiles carry any value, so no
power hypothesis survives either. Left unnamed; documented on `SimGridSubfile`.

### The negative result: no save stores ANY simulated field

With the twins reassigned to flammability, every 128×128 layer in the shipped saves is
accounted for (traffic ×5 + six all-zero siblings, occupant codes, flammability ×2, zone
type, the power-ish pair, and constant/flag layers). **There is no saved air pollution,
land value, crime or desirability grid** — SC4 recomputes them all at load, exactly as §12
established for land value alone. Consequence for the plan's "saved grids are ground
truth" principle: pollution and crime are gated on STRUCTURE (dirty industry outpollutes
residential — zone 7 farms are net absorbers and must not count as industry; $ outscores
$$$; byte-identical fields under edit-free ticks; razing a polluting lot lowers the field
at its tile), and land value on thresholded-wealth agreement, fitted offline across all
populated saves (base 5 / neighbourhood-wealth ×45 / pollution −30; mean 0.82, worst
0.57; harness floor 0.50). Traffic assignment IS gated against a saved target
(`TRAFFIC_CAR`): precision 0.94–1.00, volume rank correlation 0.14–0.94 across saves
(floors 0.85 / 0.10).

Data-view wiring that fell out of this: "Maximum scale" (0x4A0B47EC) is now parsed — the
Air Pollution view declares 1024 with ramp stops 128..255, so the field lives in 0..1024
and maps linearly onto the stop range; Crime and Police share data-source enum 4, so those
